      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to **5,100 mg/day**. The FDA-labeled maximum is **2,550 mg/day** for immediate-release metformin, and many references use 2,000 mg/day as the usual ceiling. This order is about twice the maximum. Metformin overdose raises the risk of lactic acidosis, and that risk applies even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nPossible intended orders include:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the labeled maximum)\n- **1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals** (2,000 mg/day)\n- **500 mg PO three times daily with meals** (1,500 mg/day)\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg twice daily\n\nPlease confirm the intended dose and frequency. If you really do want 1,700 mg three times daily, tell me and include a clinical rationale. I would still suggest checking it with pharmacy first."
      }
